"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Preoperative PSA was 5.4. The surgical findings included a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2), pT3a stage with extraprostatic extension, positive surgical margins, and no seminal vesicle invasion or lymphovascular invasion. The absence of lymph node removal and the lack of documented nodal sampling widen the uncertainty regarding nodal status. Biopsy findings matched the prostatectomy specimen.\n\nCountervailing factors include the positive surgical margins and the T3a stage. The absence of documented postoperative PSA or follow-up significantly limits the ability to assess the trajectory of recurrence. Missing nodal sampling further complicates the assessment of regional disease control. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and subsequent trajectory would be crucial to revise this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 62.93 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 37.76–88.10 months; its coverage has not been validated."
